# Cloudflare Pages redirects. Parsed by Pages — never served as a file itself.
#
# What does NOT belong in this file: domain-level redirects. Pages does not support them here
# (`workers.example.com/* ... 301` is explicitly unsupported), so the canonical-host rule
# www.barchinesca.club -> barchinesca.club has to be a Redirect Rule in the Cloudflare
# dashboard. Only path rules work below.
#
# Why the .html rules exist: Pages already serves extensionless URLs and sends
# /galeria.html -> /galeria by itself, but as a 307 (temporary). Stating the same destination
# here makes it a 301 (permanent), so search engines settle on one address per page instead of
# treating /galeria and /galeria.html as two.
#
# Format: [source] [destination] [code]

/index.html     /        301

/galeria.html   /galeria  301
/login.html     /login    301
/profile.html   /profile  301
/cancel.html    /cancel   301
/privacy.html   /privacy  301
